 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "The electronic configuration lists the electrons in each shell, inner to outer: 2, 8, 1 for sodium.\nRule for the first 20: fill 2, then 8, then 8, then the rest.\n• H 1 · He 2 · Li 2,1 · Be 2,2 · B 2,3 · C 2,4 · N 2,5 · O 2,6 · F 2,7 · Ne 2,8\n• Na 2,8,1 · Mg 2,8,2 · Al 2,8,3 · Si 2,8,4 · P 2,8,5 · S 2,8,6 · Cl 2,8,7 · Ar 2,8,8 · K 2,8,8,1 · Ca 2,8,8,2\nThe total of the numbers equals the atomic number.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "learn": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "sections": [
   {
    "heading": "Writing configurations",
    "text": "The electronic configuration lists the number of electrons in each shell from the nucleus outwards, separated by commas.\nMethod: start with the atomic number, put {2} in the first shell, up to {8} in the second, up to {8} in the third, and the rest in the fourth.\nPhosphorus ({15}): {2}, {8}, {5}. Check: {2} + {8} + {5} = {15}."
   },
   {
    "heading": "The first twenty",
    "text": "• H {1} · He {2}\n• Li {2},{1} · Be {2},{2} · B {2},{3} · C {2},{4} · N {2},{5} · O {2},{6} · F {2},{7} · Ne {2},{8}\n• Na {2},{8},{1} · Mg {2},{8},{2} · Al {2},{8},{3} · Si {2},{8},{4} · P {2},{8},{5} · S {2},{8},{6} · Cl {2},{8},{7} · Ar {2},{8},{8}\n• K {2},{8},{8},{1} · Ca {2},{8},{8},{2}\nNotice the pattern repeating in each row."
   },
   {
    "heading": "Configurations of ions",
    "text": "When an atom becomes an ion, only the electrons change.\n• Na ({2},{8},{1}) loses {1} → Na⁺ {2},{8}.\n• Cl ({2},{8},{7}) gains {1} → Cl⁻ {2},{8},{8}.\nBoth ions end up with a full outer shell, like a noble gas. This is the key to chemical bonding."
   }
  ],
  "key_words": [
   {
    "word": "electronic configuration",
    "meaning": "the number of electrons in each shell, e.g. {2}, {8}, {1}"
   },
   {
    "word": "noble gas configuration",
    "meaning": "a full outer shell, like He, Ne or Ar"
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   "Nitrogen ({7}): {2}, {5}",
   "Silicon ({14}): {2}, {8}, {4}",
   "Mg²⁺: {2}, {8}"
  ],
  "mistake": {
   "wrong": "Potassium ({19}): {2}, {8}, {9}",
   "right": "Potassium: {2}, {8}, {8}, {1}",
   "why": "For the first {20} elements the third shell holds {8} before the fourth starts."
  }
 },
